# --- Data pipeline (read from this file) ---
# DarkFinder data pipeline uses Google Earth Engine.
# Authentication is handled via `earthengine authenticate` (run once).
# Set your GCP project ID (must have Earth Engine API enabled):
GEE_PROJECT=your-gcp-project-id

# --- API server (NOT read from this file) ---
# The serving layer reads these from the process environment only. Nothing calls
# load_dotenv() at API startup and uvicorn is not given --env-file, so setting them
# here has no effect on `make dev-backend` — export them in your shell, or set them
# as service variables in Railway.
#
# FRONTEND_ORIGINS  Comma-separated exact CORS origins. Defaults to
#                   http://localhost:5173. Any localhost/127.0.0.1 port is also
#                   allowed automatically in dev via LOCALHOST_ORIGIN_REGEX
#                   (app/config.py), so this is really only needed in production,
#                   e.g. FRONTEND_ORIGINS=https://dark-finder.vercel.app
# EMISSION_COG_URL  Override the emission COG with a remote URL (e.g. R2 /vsicurl).
#                   Unset, the newest backend/data/processed/<year>_cog.tif is used.
# SKYGLOW_COG_URL   Same, for <year>_skyglow_cog.tif.
